WEBVTT

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.960
Absent-minded, I only prayed to the stars

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:27.760
Losing sight of all that was precious

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.600
Absent-minded, I kept my eyes fixed on the same spot

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:38.310
And came to a standstill myself

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.480
We don't need no reasons

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.570
To change for the better

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:55.870
Now, let's dream to the extreme

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:57.960
You're a shooting star

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.250
Kick open the doors that stand in your way

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.470
And leap beyond the infinite horizon

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.550
Light on the shooting star

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:14.560
Don't look back; what you seek is in front of you

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.680
Let's go in search of it

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.440
Fly away

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.190
Here comes a high-grade towel, oink.

00:01:44.858 --> 00:01:47.861
There, there, Doronjo.

00:01:57.204 --> 00:02:00.207
She must’ve been exhausted
since we’ve been traveling.

00:02:00.207 --> 00:02:03.210
She should rest a little…

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.837
…just like in those days.

00:02:05.837 --> 00:02:08.548
Mom, you’ll get sick, too.

00:02:08.548 --> 00:02:11.718
Don’t worry. I'm strong, you know.

00:02:11.718 --> 00:02:15.013
I’ll always protect you.

00:02:24.564 --> 00:02:25.857
Mom?

00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:29.402
What is it, Doronjo?

00:02:29.402 --> 00:02:31.112
Never mind.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.245
As expected, she misses her mom.

00:02:38.245 --> 00:02:41.039
Yeah, she’s only nine years old, so…

00:02:41.039 --> 00:02:45.126
I wish we could be the replacement for her mom.

00:02:45.126 --> 00:02:46.628
I wish I could be…

00:02:46.628 --> 00:02:49.130
…nursed like that!

00:02:51.591 --> 00:02:53.760
You have a high fever!

00:02:59.975 --> 00:03:02.310
Now, open wide!

00:03:05.772 --> 00:03:07.399
One thousand eleven!

00:03:07.399 --> 00:03:09.776
One thousand twelve!

00:03:09.776 --> 00:03:11.945
It’s quite hard to catch a cold.

00:03:11.945 --> 00:03:14.739
Boyayan, let’s pour more water over ourselves.

00:03:14.739 --> 00:03:17.284
They say stupid people don’t catch a cold, so…

00:03:17.284 --> 00:03:19.577
Then we should catch colds just fine!

00:03:19.577 --> 00:03:21.329
Yeah!

00:03:21.329 --> 00:03:26.251
We’re completely comfortable with
being Boyacky and Tonzra now, aren’t we?

00:03:26.251 --> 00:03:27.961
We are!

00:03:29.796 --> 00:03:33.466
They must be up to something naughty.

00:03:33.466 --> 00:03:35.760
Mr. Boyacky! Mr. Tonzra!

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.679
Ah, Gatchan! Welcome back!

00:03:37.679 --> 00:03:39.097
How did it go?

00:03:39.097 --> 00:03:41.349
Just as I thought, there was no one there,

00:03:41.349 --> 00:03:44.477
although it appeared that people had
lived in those houses up until recently.

00:03:44.477 --> 00:03:45.729
That’s a mystery.

00:03:45.729 --> 00:03:47.564
Yeah.

00:03:47.564 --> 00:03:49.482
I found a map there.

00:03:49.482 --> 00:03:53.403
Looks like there’s a
big lake upstream from here.

00:03:53.403 --> 00:03:56.156
There’s another town there. Let’s see…

00:03:56.156 --> 00:03:58.158
Lake Kussharo-Dessharo?

00:03:58.158 --> 00:04:00.535
That’s the lake with the Kussie legend.

00:04:00.535 --> 00:04:02.287
Kussie?

00:04:02.287 --> 00:04:05.582
It’s a legend that says that a
monster from ancient times is still alive.

00:04:05.582 --> 00:04:08.209
Monsters don’t exist.

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:09.627
Yeah, I know.

00:04:09.627 --> 00:04:11.963
It wasn’t many, but I did catch some fish.

00:04:11.963 --> 00:04:14.841
I thought I’d have Doronjo eat some.

00:04:15.925 --> 00:04:17.594
Gatchan really is…

00:04:17.594 --> 00:04:19.929
…good-hearted!

00:04:19.929 --> 00:04:22.015
Now, open wide!

00:04:25.018 --> 00:04:26.186
It’s yummy.

00:04:26.186 --> 00:04:28.188
Ally made it.

00:04:29.397 --> 00:04:32.525
She’s a good cook.

00:04:32.525 --> 00:04:34.611
This is simple rice porridge
that doesn’t even have scallions in it,

00:04:34.611 --> 00:04:39.157
but eat a lot and get well soon. Now, open wide!

00:04:45.121 --> 00:04:47.040
I wonder if you got warmer…

00:04:56.049 --> 00:04:59.052
Yes, it definitely seems like
your fever has gotten worse.

00:04:59.052 --> 00:05:01.888
Once you finish eating,
you should lie down right away.

00:05:01.888 --> 00:05:03.807
Y-Yeah, I’ll do that.

00:05:03.807 --> 00:05:06.017
Now, open wide.

00:05:08.895 --> 00:05:11.272
Gatchan is quite slow, isn’t he?

00:05:11.272 --> 00:05:14.484
He’s too clueless about girls’ feelings.

00:05:14.484 --> 00:05:20.740
Miss Doronjo had never met a
boy close to her own age before, so…

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:22.200
Dad…

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.410
"Dad"?

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:27.414
I wonder if this is how a dad who
watches over his daughter feels like…

00:05:27.414 --> 00:05:30.125
Yeah, it may be…

00:05:30.125 --> 00:05:31.751
Thank you for the food.

00:05:31.751 --> 00:05:34.754
Good. You ate it all.

00:05:34.754 --> 00:05:36.881
It would’ve been better if we had scallions.

00:05:38.341 --> 00:05:41.428
You sweat quite a bit. I’ll wipe it off for you.

00:05:43.638 --> 00:05:45.265
H-H-Hey, G-Gatchan?!

00:05:45.265 --> 00:05:47.600
What’s the matter? Don’t be shy.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.185
I-I can do it myself!

00:05:49.185 --> 00:05:50.562
You’ll miss some spots if you do it yourself.

00:05:50.562 --> 00:05:52.147
I-I won’t!

00:05:52.147 --> 00:05:53.314
Boy, he is slow.

00:05:53.314 --> 00:05:55.942
Yeah. Good thing that we didn’t have scallions.

00:05:55.942 --> 00:05:56.776
Scallions?

00:05:56.776 --> 00:06:00.280
People stick them in their butts,
saying that it’ll help cure a cold!

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.573
They cram’em right in there!

00:06:01.573 --> 00:06:04.534
Then, as dads, we definitely
can’t allow that to happen!

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:05.660
Exactly!

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.121
I-I’ll ask Alouette to do it!

00:06:08.121 --> 00:06:09.622
Seriously, where’d you go, Alouette?!

00:06:09.622 --> 00:06:12.542
I think she’s already gone to get some water.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:19.549
Cold!

00:06:21.718 --> 00:06:24.471
Stupid Gatchan.

00:06:24.471 --> 00:06:28.683
I’m gonna catch a cold like this, oink!

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:31.978
Gatchan…

00:06:31.978 --> 00:06:33.021
Hm?

00:06:33.021 --> 00:06:37.650
Could you… hold my hand for a while?

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.194
Your hand?

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:43.490
M-My hands are cold, so…

00:06:51.664 --> 00:06:54.792
Maybe it’s because of her fever…
she’s really acting like a baby.

00:06:54.792 --> 00:06:56.211
Yeah.

00:06:56.211 --> 00:07:00.006
When you do that,
you’ll feel very embarrassed later.

00:07:00.006 --> 00:07:02.550
We’re not gonna allow the scallions!

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:06.429
Mr. Gorozo used to stroke
Ally’s hands when she caught a cold.

00:07:06.429 --> 00:07:08.056
Mr. Gorozo?

00:07:08.056 --> 00:07:09.849
That’s Ally’s dad.

00:07:13.728 --> 00:07:18.191
He’d stay up all night to care for her.

00:07:18.191 --> 00:07:20.443
Sounds like he was a good dad.

00:07:20.443 --> 00:07:24.781
Mr. Gorozo truly adored her.

00:07:24.781 --> 00:07:29.369
He said, "She’s the apple
of my eye. She’s my angel".

00:07:29.369 --> 00:07:31.663
Angel…

00:07:31.663 --> 00:07:35.667
When he was being taken away by
the Yatter soldiers, he said to me,

00:07:35.667 --> 00:07:42.006
"Protect Alouette. I'm counting
on you", over and over again.

00:07:43.049 --> 00:07:46.177
What was your dad like?

00:07:46.177 --> 00:07:47.720
I don’t know.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.055
Huh?

00:07:50.765 --> 00:07:55.019
Before I was born, he…

00:07:55.019 --> 00:07:56.563
I see…

00:07:56.563 --> 00:07:59.816
M-Miss Doronjo, you can call me Dad.

00:07:59.816 --> 00:08:02.860
You can call me Mom!

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:05.530
You should get some sleep now.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:06.447
Yeah.

00:08:06.447 --> 00:08:07.240
I'm your dad!

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.074
I'm your mom!

00:08:08.074 --> 00:08:08.658
I'm your dad.

00:08:08.658 --> 00:08:09.909
--Tell me a story.
--I'm your mom.

00:08:09.909 --> 00:08:10.785
--Tell me a story.
--I'm your dad.

00:08:10.785 --> 00:08:11.661
--Tell me a story.
--I'm your mom.

00:08:11.661 --> 00:08:12.328
--A story, huh…
--I'm your dad.

00:08:12.328 --> 00:08:13.371
--A story, huh…
--I'm your mom.

00:08:13.371 --> 00:08:14.205
I'm your dad.

00:08:14.205 --> 00:08:15.248
I'm your mom.

00:08:15.248 --> 00:08:16.124
--Have you ever played with a ball and cup?
--I'm your dad.

00:08:16.124 --> 00:08:17.125
--Have you ever played with a ball and cup?
--I'm your mom.

00:08:17.125 --> 00:08:17.542
--Have you ever played with a ball and cup?
--I'm your dad.

00:08:17.542 --> 00:08:19.043
No.

00:08:19.043 --> 00:08:23.965
l only played it when I was small,
but I’ll make a set for you some time.

00:08:23.965 --> 00:08:25.174
Okay.

00:08:25.174 --> 00:08:26.092
I'm your mom.

00:08:26.092 --> 00:08:27.719
I'm your…

00:08:27.719 --> 00:08:32.181
We’ve come quite far.

00:08:32.181 --> 00:08:35.852
The legendary thief group Doronbow,

00:08:35.852 --> 00:08:38.771
which consists of Doronjo, Tonzra and Boyacky…

00:08:38.771 --> 00:08:41.733
And their boss Dokurobey…

00:08:41.733 --> 00:08:45.278
In this picture book, Yatterman is the hero,

00:08:45.278 --> 00:08:47.864
and Doronbow is the villain.

00:08:47.864 --> 00:08:49.949
But in reality, it’s the complete opposite.

00:08:49.949 --> 00:08:53.244
Yatter Kingdom is hell on earth.

00:08:53.244 --> 00:08:57.707
And those who call themselves
Doronbow are the heroes.

00:08:57.707 --> 00:09:00.335
Heroes…

00:09:00.335 --> 00:09:02.003
I'm talking about you guys, Doronjo.

00:09:02.003 --> 00:09:06.591
You’re trying to bring down
Yatterman for those who are suffering.

00:09:06.591 --> 00:09:09.469
Heroes, huh…?

00:09:09.469 --> 00:09:11.888
But that includes you, too, Gatchan.

00:09:11.888 --> 00:09:14.015
I'm not doing anything.

00:09:14.015 --> 00:09:19.812
That’s not true. I'm very
glad that we can travel together.

00:09:19.812 --> 00:09:21.689
I'm glad to hear that.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.903
Gatchan, I like--

00:09:26.903 --> 00:09:29.656
I wonder what’s keeping Alouette…

00:09:29.656 --> 00:09:32.533
Good night!

00:09:32.533 --> 00:09:33.993
Good night.

00:09:33.993 --> 00:09:35.453
He really is slow.

00:09:35.453 --> 00:09:37.163
Don’t let your guard down.

00:09:37.163 --> 00:09:40.124
He’s watching for the scallion chance!

00:09:48.508 --> 00:09:51.678
You came to bathe in the river, too, Gatchan?

00:09:51.678 --> 00:09:53.471
Gatchan?

00:10:01.437 --> 00:10:04.482
Mr. Boyacky? Mr. Tonzra?

00:10:04.482 --> 00:10:06.025
Since Miss Alouette has
been gone for a while now,

00:10:06.025 --> 00:10:07.777
we’ll go check on her.

00:10:07.777 --> 00:10:09.654
Wait. I’ll go with you.

00:10:09.654 --> 00:10:11.447
You don’t have to come.

00:10:11.447 --> 00:10:12.532
That’s right.

00:10:12.532 --> 00:10:13.950
I’ll come along, too.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.953
We’re not thinking that Miss Alouette…

00:10:16.953 --> 00:10:18.871
…might be bathing in the river or anything.

00:10:18.871 --> 00:10:20.623
I bet you are.

00:10:20.623 --> 00:10:21.708
We aren’t.

00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:22.875
You are.

00:10:22.875 --> 00:10:25.378
We aren’t.

00:10:30.174 --> 00:10:32.385
Feels nice and cold…

00:10:38.891 --> 00:10:42.770
Seriously, this isn’t possible.

00:10:46.065 --> 00:10:48.151
Whoa!

00:10:52.697 --> 00:10:55.283
Good morning, Doronjo, Kutchan!

00:10:55.283 --> 00:10:57.618
K-K-K-K-Kutchan?!

00:10:58.619 --> 00:11:00.496
It smells nice, doesn’t it?

00:11:00.496 --> 00:11:05.251
M-M-M-M-Monster!

00:11:09.531 --> 00:11:12.784
The monster Kussie in Lake Kussharo-Dessharo?!

00:11:12.784 --> 00:11:14.369
Seems like he’s its child.

00:11:14.369 --> 00:11:16.913
There’s no way Kussie really exists!

00:11:16.913 --> 00:11:19.708
Here, I’ll give you fish bones!
--You may say so, but it actually exists, so…

00:11:19.708 --> 00:11:20.709
Here, I’ll give you fish bones!
--Yes, it does.

00:11:20.709 --> 00:11:22.252
It does.

00:11:22.252 --> 00:11:24.170
You’re accepting this too easily!

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:24.838
But not like you.

00:11:24.838 --> 00:11:26.214
--Not like you.
--Not like you.

00:11:26.214 --> 00:11:28.842
I-I’m not accepting it easily!

00:11:28.842 --> 00:11:33.263
I was surprised when I saw
Miss Alouette was with Kutchan.

00:11:36.099 --> 00:11:39.602
It was too bad that she
was already dressed, though.

00:11:41.146 --> 00:11:43.231
Why is he covered with cuts and bruises?

00:11:43.231 --> 00:11:47.068
According to the story
Miss Alouette heard from Kutchan…

00:11:48.695 --> 00:11:53.533
…it seems like he was attacked by
Yatter soldiers at Lake Kussharo-Dessharo.

00:11:53.533 --> 00:11:54.617
By Yatter soldiers?

00:11:54.617 --> 00:11:56.578
It’s terrible.

00:11:56.578 --> 00:11:59.414
He has injuries from guns and
swords, as well as electric burns…

00:11:59.414 --> 00:12:04.252
He was attacked at the lake and
drifted into the river, too weak to swim…

00:12:04.252 --> 00:12:06.421
Are you hurting, Kutchan?

00:12:10.633 --> 00:12:12.635
Oh, I see. You want to see your mom.

00:12:12.635 --> 00:12:14.262
There, there.

00:12:24.439 --> 00:12:27.692
It seems like he got separated
from his mom when he drifted.

00:12:27.692 --> 00:12:29.736
So he’s feeling sad.

00:12:29.736 --> 00:12:32.363
I see…

00:12:32.363 --> 00:12:33.990
I wish I could be the replacement…

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:35.950
…for your mom.

00:12:53.301 --> 00:12:55.386
Are you missing your mom?

00:12:56.721 --> 00:12:58.431
There, there.

00:12:58.431 --> 00:13:01.476
Yeah, I know how you feel.

00:13:01.476 --> 00:13:03.311
You feel lonely, don’t you?

00:13:08.525 --> 00:13:10.568
We feel lonely.

00:13:15.573 --> 00:13:18.660
We’re gonna take him to
Lake Kussharo-Dessharo?!

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:21.788
We’re gonna take Kutchan to his mom!

00:13:21.788 --> 00:13:22.580
But…

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:25.166
There are Yatter soldiers
at Lake Kussharo-Dessharo!

00:13:25.166 --> 00:13:27.168
So what?!

00:13:27.168 --> 00:13:28.503
It’s dangerous!

00:13:28.503 --> 00:13:30.922
The feelings of a child wanting
to see his mom are far more important

00:13:30.922 --> 00:13:34.717
than whether there are
Yatter soldiers there or not!

00:13:34.717 --> 00:13:38.555
I’m sure his mom wants to see hi--

00:13:38.555 --> 00:13:39.222
Doronjo!

00:13:39.222 --> 00:13:40.807
Miss Doronjo!

00:13:43.601 --> 00:13:45.436
You understand it, don’t you?

00:13:45.436 --> 00:13:48.022
I do.

00:13:48.022 --> 00:13:49.190
Ally…

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:55.071
My dad, mom, and dog are
waiting for me to come see them.

00:13:55.071 --> 00:13:57.407
Yeah, that’s right.

00:13:57.407 --> 00:14:01.327
I understand. If I were Miss Doronjo’s dad…

00:14:01.327 --> 00:14:05.081
…I'd want to see her at any risk!

00:14:05.081 --> 00:14:07.292
You can call me "Dad"!

00:14:07.292 --> 00:14:09.419
You can call me "Mom"!

00:14:09.419 --> 00:14:11.671
You can!

00:14:11.671 --> 00:14:13.298
Let’s go, you guys!

00:14:13.298 --> 00:14:15.258
Yes, ma’am!

00:14:15.258 --> 00:14:16.259
l couldn’t hear you guys!

00:14:16.259 --> 00:14:18.678
Yes, ma’am!

00:14:25.894 --> 00:14:27.103
You can call me "Dad".

00:14:27.103 --> 00:14:28.563
You can call me "Mom".

00:14:28.563 --> 00:14:31.524
Would you quit that?!

00:14:31.524 --> 00:14:38.406
Dad, huh? Then, Alouette would be my mom?

00:14:38.406 --> 00:14:41.117
Which means…

00:14:41.117 --> 00:14:42.744
I'm home!

00:14:42.744 --> 00:14:44.913
l managed to catch a big rabbit!

00:14:44.913 --> 00:14:49.000
Welcome home!
Then we’ll have rabbit soup tonight!

00:14:54.213 --> 00:14:57.425
Oh, the thought makes me blush!

00:14:57.425 --> 00:14:58.801
But…

00:14:58.801 --> 00:15:00.720
Are you okay, Ally?

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.347
I'm fine!

00:15:02.347 --> 00:15:05.642
Of course, Gatchan’s like that.

00:15:05.642 --> 00:15:10.313
Besides, I wonder if the day
when the whole family can live

00:15:10.313 --> 00:15:14.067
happily together in peace will really come…

00:15:14.067 --> 00:15:17.946
Maybe I’ll act like a spoiled child
a little, at least for now.

00:15:17.946 --> 00:15:19.739
That’s okay, right?

00:15:19.739 --> 00:15:21.532
Hm? ls something wrong?

00:15:21.532 --> 00:15:25.286
Oh, nothing! Never mind, meow!

00:15:25.286 --> 00:15:28.081
l said "meow," meow

00:15:28.081 --> 00:15:29.999
With the warmth that a dad would have…

00:15:29.999 --> 00:15:33.044
…we’ll be watching over you.

00:15:33.044 --> 00:15:36.589
ln any case, he’d better
not be looking for scallions.

00:15:36.589 --> 00:15:39.175
Looks like there are no Yatter soldiers.

00:15:39.175 --> 00:15:41.469
Doronjo, we’re almost there.

00:15:42.553 --> 00:15:46.808
If we go up there, we should be able
to look over Lake Kussharo-Dessharo…

00:15:46.808 --> 00:15:49.060
…to see what on earth happened…

00:15:50.812 --> 00:15:53.606
Hm? What? You’ve already started recording?

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.819
I go there and whisper. I come here and whisper.

00:15:57.819 --> 00:15:59.612
This is Whispering Reporter.

00:15:59.612 --> 00:16:03.992
What on earth happened
at Lake Kussharo-Dessharo?

00:16:03.992 --> 00:16:08.496
We witnessed the entire incident.

00:16:08.496 --> 00:16:11.958
Please look at this. More people are being
taken away from the village by the lake.

00:16:11.958 --> 00:16:15.336
Looks like they’re all evicted from the village.

00:16:15.336 --> 00:16:18.756
You should be happy that
you’re able to offer the land.

00:16:18.756 --> 00:16:23.511
We’ll build a factory for Lord Yatterman
at Lake Kussharo-Dessharo!

00:16:23.511 --> 00:16:25.346
Yatterman!

00:16:26.973 --> 00:16:29.267
We’ve completed taking the residents away!

00:16:29.267 --> 00:16:31.894
Good. Things are going smoothly.

00:16:35.231 --> 00:16:39.902
Oh! Is that the legendary monster
Kussie of Lake Kussharo-Dessharo?!

00:16:39.902 --> 00:16:42.447
It’s angry! It’s going on a rampage!

00:16:42.447 --> 00:16:45.533
I can see a small Kussie, too!
Looks like it’s a baby Kussie!

00:16:45.533 --> 00:16:46.659
Kussie?!

00:16:46.659 --> 00:16:49.954
I’ll show no mercy to those who stand
in our way, no matter who they are!

00:16:49.954 --> 00:16:51.622
Capture them!

00:16:59.297 --> 00:17:02.383
Geez, it caused me a lot of trouble.

00:17:04.594 --> 00:17:08.097
They say that Kussie was living
in harmony with the residents,

00:17:08.097 --> 00:17:11.392
so it attacked those who
were taking the residents away.

00:17:11.392 --> 00:17:14.395
This report was brought to
you by Whispering Reporter.

00:17:14.395 --> 00:17:16.481
Hm?! Please hold on a second!

00:17:16.481 --> 00:17:17.815
They’re…

00:17:18.816 --> 00:17:20.943
How terrible…

00:17:20.943 --> 00:17:22.612
Is that your mom?

00:17:24.113 --> 00:17:25.907
We have to save her.

00:17:25.907 --> 00:17:27.492
Boyacky! Tonzra!

00:17:27.492 --> 00:17:29.410
Yes, ma’am!

00:17:31.871 --> 00:17:34.207
Take his!

00:17:50.515 --> 00:17:51.641
They are…

00:17:51.682 --> 00:17:52.600
Capture them!

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:53.893
Yatterman!

00:17:53.893 --> 00:17:56.687
We were able to secure the land for a factory.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:02.568
And, now, we’re capering Doronjo and her gang!

00:18:02.568 --> 00:18:04.904
This is, indeed,
killing three birds with one stone!

00:18:04.904 --> 00:18:08.199
This’ll allow me to save my
honor in front of Lord Yatterman!

00:18:11.285 --> 00:18:12.912
I-I’m sorry.

00:18:12.912 --> 00:18:14.497
You can apologize later.

00:18:14.497 --> 00:18:16.874
Boyacky! Hurry up and <i>click!</i>

00:18:16.874 --> 00:18:19.460
Well, I haven't built anything yet!

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:20.795
Yatter!

00:18:21.838 --> 00:18:23.297
Gatchan!

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:27.468
Yatterpug!

00:18:29.428 --> 00:18:31.597
Here’s the Mecha Tonic!

00:18:40.648 --> 00:18:44.402
Sticky, sticky… Sticky, sticky…

00:18:44.402 --> 00:18:47.113
Sticky Nets! Fire the nets!

00:18:47.113 --> 00:18:56.581
Sticky, sticky, sticky!
Sticky, sticky, sticky!

00:18:56.581 --> 00:18:58.666
Eww! It’s sticky!

00:18:58.666 --> 00:19:00.626
I-I-I can’t move!

00:19:00.626 --> 00:19:02.295
This is nothing!

00:19:02.295 --> 00:19:04.922
Hm? I can’t tear it open!

00:19:04.922 --> 00:19:06.549
A-Ally, are you okay?l

00:19:06.591 --> 00:19:08.509
What are you talking about?

00:19:08.509 --> 00:19:10.928
How rude, oink!

00:19:10.928 --> 00:19:12.513
Gulp.

00:19:13.347 --> 00:19:16.517
You can’t escape now!

00:19:16.517 --> 00:19:22.356
I'm gonna make you regret going
against Lord Yatterman big time!

00:19:22.356 --> 00:19:25.484
That zings!

00:19:29.906 --> 00:19:32.366
Time to finish you off!

00:19:36.537 --> 00:19:38.873
Laven… der…?

00:19:42.668 --> 00:19:44.378
General Goro?

00:19:53.679 --> 00:19:55.473
It’s no use!

00:19:55.473 --> 00:19:58.142
That net cannot be torn off!

00:20:03.648 --> 00:20:05.650
Wh-What?!

00:20:23.542 --> 00:20:25.544
Sh-She’s strong…

00:20:28.089 --> 00:20:32.426
Wow… Trust a mom to be strong.

00:20:38.349 --> 00:20:39.934
Take care!

00:20:39.934 --> 00:20:41.644
Good bye!

00:20:41.644 --> 00:20:45.690
Don’t get separated from your mom again!

00:20:49.485 --> 00:20:52.488
Live happily together forever.

00:20:52.488 --> 00:20:54.575
Look on me as your dad
and let’s be happy together.

00:20:54.575 --> 00:20:56.675
Look on me as your mom
and let’s be happy together.

00:20:57.576 --> 00:20:58.911
Are you okay?

00:20:58.911 --> 00:21:03.791
Y-Yeah… I feel a little better… I think.

00:21:03.791 --> 00:21:05.501
Good…

00:21:06.294 --> 00:21:07.962
Scallions!

00:21:07.962 --> 00:21:09.588
I’ll use these scallions and…

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:10.965
Gatchan’s got scallions!

00:21:10.965 --> 00:21:14.302
He’s gonna stick them in her butt!
We gotta stop him!

00:21:14.302 --> 00:21:16.345
The rice porridge will be tastier with them.

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:22.268
Scallions…

00:21:22.268 --> 00:21:23.811
They look like Kutchan.

00:21:23.811 --> 00:21:25.855
Scallion-miso, oink!

00:21:33.904 --> 00:21:39.160
Yo-ho! Yo-ho! Yo-ho! Yo-ho! Yo-ho…!

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:42.663
Doronjo! I'm glad that you feel better!

00:21:42.663 --> 00:21:44.582
Y-Yeah!

00:21:45.499 --> 00:21:47.001
I can’t believe I did it!

00:21:47.001 --> 00:21:51.297
I just felt weak… acted like a baby,
and said stuff like "meow"!

00:21:51.297 --> 00:21:53.924
What’s "meow"?! Why did I say "meow"?!

00:21:53.924 --> 00:21:54.216
Yo ho! Yo-ho! Yo-ho…!

00:21:54.216 --> 00:21:57.053
What the heck, meow?!

00:21:57.053 --> 00:21:59.263
H-Hey!

00:21:59.263 --> 00:22:00.848
Doronjo?

00:22:00.848 --> 00:22:02.558
Doronjo?!

00:22:02.558 --> 00:22:08.064
What meow the heck is "meow",meow?!

